warhawk92@gmail.com writes:

> How would I go about patching Nethack/SLASH 'EM?

Get the source packet, unpack it, use the patch utility to apply the
patches and compile. 
But I suggest first compiling the game as it comes from the packet before
beginning to apply patches. That way it will be easier to narrow the
causes of any possible problems you may encounter. See the sys directory
in the source tree and particularly the subdirectory there for your
platform for more instructions. 

> There's a couple patches I'd like to apply (user-created ones), but I
> have no idea where to start. Help?

If the instructions above and the ones in the sys directory of the source
tree are not clear enough, you should start by telling which operating
system you want to compile the game for. 

